{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar","id":974131,"title":"What is an Avatar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-21T17:30:20-07:00","id":974131,"title":"What is an Avatar?","content":"What exactly is a mages avatar? Mages(and to a lesser extent, mummies) themselves seem to believe that they're some fundamental part of the soul, but at the same time there are cases where avatars seem to be able to exist separate from the soul of the mage or even leave at will. For instance, if a mage becomes a vampire it is said their avatar moves on, but vampires themselves are shown to retain their souls. The winged deamon in dark ages is another example, it was apparently &quot;thrown out&quot; by her mage when he grew tired of her. Yet another is the flaw &quot;Ban&quot;, in which one of the punishments for violating your character's ban was your avatar getting fed up and leaving your mage character(taking their true magic with them).<br /> <br /> Considering that avatars are also(supposedly) the source of a mages True Magick, does that mean that awakening isn't the mage seeing their own true potential, but instead being shown said potential by an outside entity that then &quot;Moves In&quot;? What about the consensus, is the reason for it because humans can't control their ability to manipulate reality without a helping hand?<br /> <br /> Also acknowledging that ascension is something that avatars are pushing their mage towards, is it truely the mage's ascention or the avatar's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:41:50-07:00","id":974136,"title":"","content":"All of these are <i>excellent</i> questions.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately (or Fortunately), this being Mage: The Ascension, not only are these questions mostly not answered, but the potential answers could all be true at the same time.<br /> <br /> Is the Avatar the same thing as the Soul? A different aspect of a multi-part Soul? A revered ancestor or Totem? A figment of one's subconscious? A fragment of the divine, seeking to push the Mage towards a reconciliation and merging with the Most High? Some sort of spirit that attaches itself to sapient beings, giving them the potential for True Magick in return for a vessel to hang out in? A guardian angel?<br /> <br /> Who knows? Mages of every stripe have certainly spent a considerable amount of time arguing the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T20:09:26-07:00","id":974198,"title":"","content":"&quot;Avatar&quot; is essentially Traditions magical <i>lingua franca</i> for &quot;that thing which lets us do magick&quot;. What <i>else</i> is ascribed to it may vary wildly between Traditions, but past-life memories are common, as are certain manifestations, hallucinatory or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Canonically, though, the closest we come to something resembling a definitive answer is &quot;fragments or possibly self-replicating wholes of cosmic reality-warping superweapons forged by Celestines with the power to manipulate cause and effect on a level unsurpassed by any save those who forged them, invented and given to them by one of the titans who forged the world in an act of ill-thought-out vengeance against his siblings, and designed to empower specifically human souls with the capability to fight things for which death has no meaning and nonetheless kill them&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, various canonical bits of WoD in general and Mage in particular are of dubious truthfulness, so take that with a grain of Starmetal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-21-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T04:36:05-07:00","id":974332,"title":"","content":"The <b>Ascension </b>scenario book mentions Psychopomps, which are spirits whose purpose was/is to guide the right Avatar for each Awakening human. This suggests that they are separate Spirits that attach themselves to someone during the moment of Awakening. (Or some time before, I suppose?) Spirit is the Sphere for the manipulation of Avatars. (I''d say If it would be the case of Avatar being a higher self, then it would be Prime)<br /> At the same time, there are mentions of Technocracy wanting to subdue or destroy the sleeping Avatars of the masses. But they could be wrong about this, or it could be just a metaphor for pushing their view of Consensus.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascension</b> also mentions the phenomenon of silent Avatars, which is what happens when an Avatar stops engaging the Mage. I can imagine some Mages who think they are communicating with their Avatar, that are actually talking to their higher self, while having a silent Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:29:53-07:00","id":974369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974332#post974332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>Ascension </b>scenario book mentions Psychopomps, which are spirits whose purpose was/is to guide the right Avatar for each Awakening human. This suggests that they are separate Spirits that attach themselves to someone during the moment of Awakening. (Or some time before, I suppose?) Spirit is the Sphere for the manipulation of Avatars. (I''d say If it would be the case of Avatar being a higher self, then it would be Prime)</div> </div> </div> </div>This was actually mentioned in Mage 1st Edition core, but since then was..not mentioned anymore, aside of mayhaps an early ST handbook or so. I think while originally the Psychopomp angle was supposed to be more in the foreground, the nature of avatars since then has been simply left vague and a mystery. Well, aside of the Ascension scenario book again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-22-2016, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T09:43:34-07:00","id":974474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974369#post974369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was actually mentioned in Mage 1st Edition core, but since then was..not mentioned anymore, aside of mayhaps an early ST handbook or so. I think while originally the Psychopomp angle was supposed to be more in the foreground, the nature of avatars since then has been simply left vague and a mystery. Well, aside of the Ascension scenario book again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, they popped back up in &quot;Manifesto: Transmissions from the Rogue Council,&quot; but that's just a nitpick. It was close enough to &quot;Ascension&quot; anyway.<br /> <br /> As to the question at hand, it's been pretty well addressed. There are not hard and fast definitions of what an Avatar is canonically, or even a soul for that matter. Nothing mechanically, at least. Different factions and cultures will assert different things. Some will even imply that the Avatar and the soul are one and the same. There was mention of Vampire and its relationship with souls, but we start wading into pretty murky waters when we view the metaphysics of one game through the lens of another, so I think it best to avoid. However, I do remember reading once that the Avatar is shredded upon the Embrace, and I'm inclined to use that instead of allowing the Avatar to merely detach and move on in its cosmic reincarnation cycle. It adds quite a bit of horror, I think. Although... it might be cool for a reincarnated Avatar to meet its former host who yet survives as a vampire... Even better if said vampire is a Tremere and recognizes the Avatar as formerly his and doggedly pursues it for his dark purposes... I'm going to file that idea away.<br /> <br /> It is generally accepted that Avatars are immortal in some way, and that it carries memories with it, and even retains injury to itself. The reason that Gilgul is such a frightening thing for a mage is that it's so damn permanent, both the maiming of the Avatar or its complete destruction. Carry that forward to a Nephandi's inverted Avatar: it's inverted <i>forever</i> and will reincarnate in its perverted, inverted state to continue spreading its mad ambitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:54:18-07:00","id":974528,"title":"","content":"The description of Widderslaintes suggests that Avatar are Spirits as well to me - because otherwise the Widderslaintes would be noted to be reincarnations of former Nephandi. Depending on one's outlook, this could be the case.<br /> However, from the way they are described, it seems to me that they are people to whom an inverted Avatar attached at birth. It is directly written that Widderslaintes who don't Awaken are killed so that the Avatar will travel to another person.<br /> <br /> <br /> Book of Madness also mentions that Mages can barter with their Willpower+Arete as Soul Points for Infernal Investments. When the number of Soul Points exceeds the Avatar rating, the Avatar is enslaved, and Spheres and Arete cannot be raised (cause you can't go on a Seeking, I suppose). After a few years the Demon Lord separates the Avatar from the Mage, taking away the ability to work True Magick.<br /> This is not noted as numbing the Mage the way Gilgul does, suggesting that a Mage is able to live on as a normal person, despite their Avatar being sheared off - I see it as further evidence that it is an attached Spirit, rather than an awakened part of one's being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-22-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:04:21-07:00","id":974572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974474#post974474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Although... it might be cool for a reincarnated Avatar to meet its former host who yet survives as a vampire... Even better if said vampire is a Tremere and recognizes the Avatar as formerly his and doggedly pursues it for his dark purposes... I'm going to file that idea away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been advocating this interpretation for a while now, specifically because it creates more avenues for potential stories. If the Embrace just destroys the Avatar, then that's it. No more stories are possible. But if the Avatar just leaves with the Embrace - because the Mage in question dies - then it can create any number of stories thereafter. Up to and including how the newly undead former Mage deals with their subsequent incarnations.<br /> <br /> And while there's certainly plenty of stories involving an adversarial relationship between the two, there's just as much that can be found in a non-adversarial role. The Vampire acting as a secret patron, guardian &quot;angel&quot;, mentor, magical instructor (sure, the vampire can only use blood magic himself, but he remembers how he did True Magick, right?), even surrogate parent.<br /> <br /> There are even mixes between the two extremes. The vampire may feel conflicting emotions of protectiveness and bitterness. A mentor who helps their successor, but in such a way as to also secretly use them as a pawn for political advantage. A teacher insisting that their &quot;student&quot; do magick exactly the way he used to do it, regardless of the different needs of the times. Even a patron who thinks that, if their successor doesn't meet their standards of competence, it might be better to just kill them and hope the next incarnation is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:07:12-07:00","id":974576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974528#post974528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The description of Widderslaintes suggests that Avatar are Spirits as well to me - because otherwise the Widderslaintes would be noted to be reincarnations of former Nephandi. Depending on one's outlook, this could be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's up in the air whether getting a returning Avatar counts as a reincarnation, but I'm inclined to say that whatever they are, they are a part of being human. There's certainly enough indication that the Avatar is not the soul itself, but it is an open possibility that all Sleepers have them. In some cases that is even given as the reason the Consensus has any power, the Avatars may be asleep, but they still have power. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T12:34:11-07:00","id":974598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974572#post974572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been advocating this interpretation for a while now, specifically because it creates more avenues for potential stories. If the Embrace just destroys the Avatar, then that's it. No more stories are possible. But if the Avatar just leaves with the Embrace - because the Mage in question dies - then it can create any number of stories thereafter. Up to and including how the newly undead former Mage deals with their subsequent incarnations.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was the case, I wonder whether what would be going on in regards to Avatars of the first Tremeres, especially those of the original Cainite Council of Seven members. I can see a horror story of them tracking each subsequent bearer and either Embracing or killing them - something about the Avatars providing sympathetic connection to them that can't be allowed to exist, especially in the form of someone possessing True Magick. (Let's assume they never were able to invent any sort of Gilgul ritual or get any Mage to do it) You could have a story hook with how Tremeres nudge the suspected bearers into Awakening, as only after it one can get a confirmation that it is indeed one of 'theirs' Avatars returned.<br /> Some reluctantly-Cainite Tremeres could be disobeying this directive, and protecting and nurturing the Avatars and their bearers. Possibly in hope that one day one - or a group - of them will be able to cure them of vampirism.<br /> Protecting the Avatar, if you factor the possibility of Nephandic seduction, is quite challenging. Is it better to kill a Mage than have the merest risk that they would join the Nephandi?<br /> (Widderslainte bearing an Avatar of one of the original Tremeres would be quite the snowflake to play as good-aligned Technocrat!<br /> As a Syndic, the goal would be to earn $$$ of the vampires fad and turn it into Quintessence with Primal Utility to, for a start, produce synthetic-but-tasty blood, and market it properly to the potential customers.)<br /> <br /> Similar case could be with Nagaraja. Some could be protecting and nurturing an Avatar in hope that one day at least their hunger for flesh might be lifted, somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-22-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:00:27-07:00","id":974615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974572#post974572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been advocating this interpretation for a while now, specifically because it creates more avenues for potential stories. If the Embrace just destroys the Avatar, then that's it. No more stories are possible. But if the Avatar just leaves with the Embrace - because the Mage in question dies - then it can create any number of stories thereafter. Up to and including how the newly undead former Mage deals with their subsequent incarnations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really of a couple minds on this. I do agree with you about the compelling story possibilities that can come about involving a vampire and his lost Avatar. On the other hand, I like to preserve a considerable amount of horror for mages who deal with vampires and some of the rather dire consequences involved. It's for that reason that I tend to like the rules for mage ghouldom in Blood Treachery because of simply <i>how bad </i>they hurt. <br /> <br /> I might go the route of stipulating that Avatars <i>are</i> indeed destroyed upon the Embrace, and not in a very nice way. Most of the time. Or maybe all of the time. Now that I'm thinking about it, I'm going with all of the time, but someone, maybe even the vampire/former mage himself finds a way to stitch it back together with great effort, but couldn't keep the thing nailed down and it reenters the cycle. It's still damaged in some way (possible partial Gilgul, maybe just some incoherentness and dark imagery during Seekings, or anywhere in between), but a functional, non-inverted Avatar that Awakens in a new host. Oh! And because of its history, both its host and reintigration, it's become a rather tasty treat, drawing in Nephandi to send it through the Cauls. This would likely further spur on the vampire to track down the imperiled Avatar to protect it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:39:29-07:00","id":974639,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to say how awesome this thread is! Learned a lot from it. Gave me some good ideas for my game. Thanks to all who contributed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T13:45:19-07:00","id":974642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974615#post974615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm really of a couple minds on this. I do agree with you about the compelling story possibilities that can come about involving a vampire and his lost Avatar. On the other hand, I like to preserve a considerable amount of horror for mages who deal with vampires and some of the rather dire consequences involved. It's for that reason that I tend to like the rules for mage ghouldom in Blood Treachery because of simply <i>how bad </i>they hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respectfully disagree. The very fact that the Mage loses their Avatar AT ALL is plenty horrifying. Not just because you lose the phenomenal cosmic power, but because it's like being blinded. Simple perception magick is gone, and that sort of thing has a huge impact on how the user sees the world. If you can see into the future as easily as breathing, and then suddenly can't? That's horror. (You know, <i>on top of</i> the horror of being a vampire.)<br /> <br /> Anything more than that takes it over the top, and turns the whole thing into melodrama.<br /> <br /> Moreover, I have a logical problem with the very idea that vampire Vitae has Gilgul as an inherent property. Why would this be the case? What's the rational behind this? Is it because they are Static or Entropic? Well no, because there are plenty of Mages with a whole lot of both Resonances, yet still have their magick. Is it because it's a curse from God? But some Mages think that the Avatar is a shard of the divine. Why would the divine destroy the divine? Or else, we must conclude that the fragment of divinity theory is objectively false, which screws over those groups and the players who run them.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that this idea - that vampiric blood is inherently toxic to Avatars - only really exists to prevent Mage-Vampire hybrids. It's a Doylist conceit, used to prevent OP characters like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B9za3TrVT3g\" target=\"_blank\">Dio Brando</a> from falling into the player characters' hands. But of course, if the Avatar just moves on at the moment between exanguination and revival, the result is functionally the same.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would make the idea of the Embrace destroying the Avatar an in-universe LIE, told by master Mages on both sides of the Ascension War to their students. Layering the already bad parts of pursuing vampirism with a more punitive result. It's a way of scaring the young Mages straight, so they don't even contemplate the vampire option. For all intents and purposes, the results are the same, so the elders see no danger. Except, of course, for when a former Mage meets their successor, and suddenly takes an intense interest in them.<br /> <br /> Hell, the idea of ghouldom also destroying the Avatar could be a lie too. It's not like being a slave to an undead regnant, or else a desperate vampire-hunting blood junkie, isn't already a horrible fate. The Avatar itself doesn't need to become addicted to Vitae. How would that even work, when the Avatar is a wholly spiritual being (maybe)? I'm even willing to meet Blood Treachery halfway, and say that so long as a Mage is a Ghoul, they can't increase their Arete. The focus is more on stagnation, painting ghouldom as a spiritual dead end, rather than a trap.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the mechanical price of becoming a Ghoul Mage is far, far too severe for any Mage to seriously consider it. Which, under my &quot;The Masters Are Lying&quot; scenario, is exactly the point. But it doesn't prevent a Mage from becoming a Ghoul, nor cutting off potential stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:24:46-07:00","id":974662,"title":"","content":"I always thought that was silly. Given the core rulebook in Revised has a Merit to be a ghoul. Why would there be a MERIT in mage that makes you NOT a mage?<br /> <br /> Ruined a Concept I had for a crime-fighting Ghoul Etherite who ran around beating up vampires and stealing blood. And also robbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:40:23-07:00","id":974675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974642#post974642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell, the idea of ghouldom also destroying the Avatar could be a lie too. It's not like being a slave to an undead regnant, or else a desperate vampire-hunting blood junkie, isn't already a horrible fate. The Avatar itself doesn't need to become addicted to Vitae. How would that even work, when the Avatar is a wholly spiritual being (maybe)? I'm even willing to meet Blood Treachery halfway, and say that so long as a Mage is a Ghoul, they can't increase their Arete. The focus is more on stagnation, painting ghouldom as a spiritual dead end, rather than a trap.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the mechanical price of becoming a Ghoul Mage is far, far too severe for any Mage to seriously consider it. Which, under my &quot;The Masters Are Lying&quot; scenario, is exactly the point. But it doesn't prevent a Mage from becoming a Ghoul, nor cutting off potential stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it was written as addictive and eventually harmful to the Avatar because mage-ghouls remain one of the very few crossover powergaming possibilities left. This is especially overpowering considering that the physical Disciplines and the healing being completely Paradox-free, with the only drawback being finding a source, and finding a multiple sources so as to avoid the blood bond, as long as they're knowledgable on the topic.<br /> <br /> Still, there's really few places found in WoD where you can pay with the powers of two splats in the same characters: Abominations, mage-ghouls, and mage-thralls. Maybe werewolf-thralls too. There <i>needs</i> to be some kind of mechanical deterrent to mixing these things up to deter the powergaming. I'm not sure if you saw the thread a little while back where someone was asking about a Kinfolk mage with Gnosis and Gifts who is also a Thrall to a demon and thus has a bunch of enhancements and access to demonic Lores. The Gnosis and Gifts got shot down, but there was really no argument against &quot;my wife ended up being possessed by a demon and still loved me so made me her thrall and gave me all of my Faith points worth of enhancements and Lores with no drawback and by the way through some creative interpretation of an NPC mage means I get 10 Faith points kthx.&quot; Lacking in any mechanical reasons why thralldom was bad for a mage, there was no stopping it beside saying &quot;you really shouldn't.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:20:43-07:00","id":974724,"title":"","content":"Of course I understand the powergaming issues. My assertion was that putting a lid on said powergaming was the only real reason the extra rules exist. That is, the only reason besides the in-universe hand waves, which were not terribly convincing.<br /> <br /> And I understand that powergaming is not terribly good for a game. But that's why Storytellers need to communicate with their players on the matter...as well as play out the Mage character's addiction in a serious manner. As I've stated, such a PC is a <i>junkie</i>. Even if they don't have a regnant, they are still slaves to the thirst. Storytellers need to hammer this home to the player. And the players need to recognize the double-edged sword they are running with. If either of these are impossible, then the Storyteller needs to avoid giving the player the opportunity to find vampires and easily drink from them.<br /> <br /> Plus, I already presented an alternative rule for Ghoul Mages: they cannot gain more Arete so long as they are Ghouls. They are so addicted to the Red Stuff that they lose sight of Ascension, and become so full of Stasis that they can't advance. This is at once much easier to arbitrate - you either can go on Seekings or you can't - and forces the player to choose whether they want to play a Mage or a Ghoul. Because if you have to rely on Disciplines for power, you can't advance in Magick, and vice versa. And Disciplines are much less flexible, especially at the low levels that Ghouls can use.<br /> <br /> If the Storyteller still thinks the Discipline thing is too easy, they can mandate that the Mage needs to spend blood points for every use, even if the Discipline doesn't require it. Then they need to go out hunting for vampires...or get a vampire sugar daddy. These create story possibilities, and present the character with a series of hard choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:40:05-07:00","id":974776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974642#post974642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, I have a logical problem with the very idea that vampire Vitae has Gilgul as an inherent property. Why would this be the case? What's the rational behind this? Is it because they are Static or Entropic? Well no, because there are plenty of Mages with a whole lot of both Resonances, yet still have their magick. Is it because it's a curse from God? But some Mages think that the Avatar is a shard of the divine. Why would the divine destroy the divine? Or else, we must conclude that the fragment of divinity theory is objectively false, which screws over those groups and the players who run them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there <i>is</i> that bit from Ascension that suggests that Abel was Caine's Avatar, which would mean that the first murder was also the first Gilgul. That might work as a justification, supposing one <i>were</i> to desire Avatar death as part of drinking vitae.<br /> <br /> I don't really <i>like</i> that result, it's just a possible justification. I much prefer ghouldom being an actual temptation, like Umbrood Investments are (in fact, I prefer those to be available from non-Infernal sources... actually, if you had Disciplines be a variant thereof...). The system from V20 Black Hand is actually fairly decent if you want to tell Mage Ghoul stories; it likewise blocks off Arete gains while under the influence. Or limits it by your Humanity, for Mage Revenants. I'm not sure if the experience you gain while blood-fed is actually usable for Arete, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T05:17:47-07:00","id":975002,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the mage lose his avatar when he dies before becoming a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T09:35:16-07:00","id":975096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=974598#post974598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that was the case, I wonder whether what would be going on in regards to Avatars of the first Tremeres, especially those of the original Cainite Council of Seven members. I can see a horror story of them tracking each subsequent bearer and either Embracing or killing them - something about the Avatars providing sympathetic connection to them that can't be allowed to exist, especially in the form of someone possessing True Magick. (Let's assume they never were able to invent any sort of Gilgul ritual or get any Mage to do it) You could have a story hook with how Tremeres nudge the suspected bearers into Awakening, as only after it one can get a confirmation that it is indeed one of 'theirs' Avatars returned.<br /> Some reluctantly-Cainite Tremeres could be disobeying this directive, and protecting and nurturing the Avatars and their bearers. Possibly in hope that one day one - or a group - of them will be able to cure them of vampirism.<br /> Protecting the Avatar, if you factor the possibility of Nephandic seduction, is quite challenging. Is it better to kill a Mage than have the merest risk that they would join the Nephandi?<br /> (Widderslainte bearing an Avatar of one of the original Tremeres would be quite the snowflake to play as good-aligned Technocrat!<br /> As a Syndic, the goal would be to earn $$$ of the vampires fad and turn it into Quintessence with Primal Utility to, for a start, produce synthetic-but-tasty blood, and market it properly to the potential customers.)<br /> <br /> Similar case could be with Nagaraja. Some could be protecting and nurturing an Avatar in hope that one day at least their hunger for flesh might be lifted, somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>In DA Mage, it specifically states that the &quot;quarrelsome invisible friend&quot; Avatars of Renaissance and later mages were integrated and not really separate beings. So, either they were separate beings and just weren't being chatty assholes who can decide when and how &quot;their&quot; humans use the Avatar's magic juice or the whole pre-modern phenomenon of having a separate Avatar just wasn't a thing AT ALL back when Tremere and his buddies were doing their immortality thing. <br /> <br /> In either case, it seems like a major roadblock to that story as far as the in-setting material goes. You can, of course, completely ignore it. I know I have. I ran a game once where the implicit conceit was &quot;Avatars = souls&quot; and one of the characters was the reincarnation of Tytalus. It led to a very interesting scene when the mages showed up in Vienna that involved a conversation with his &quot;brother in Art&quot;, aka Tremere-by-proxy (or, more appropriately, some of the attention of Tremere was briefly directed his way). <br /> <br /> But under the &quot;orthodoxy&quot; it would be very convoluted for Etrius, et al. to chase down an Avatar through the ages something they never were aware that they had or needed, and, upon losing, didn't really notice overmuch (sure THAT kind of magic wasn't working anymore for the newly-vamped, but they put all their accumen and knowledge to work and were able to create THIS kind of magic over here pretty damn fast.). Why wouldn't the leading Tremere consider this whole hysterical Avatar thing to represent a weakness of Will by modern mages? They have to invent some kind of imaginary playmate to handle the cognitive dissonance that being a mage creates in their mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:46:26-07:00","id":975213,"title":"","content":"Especially considering, apart from the void engineers, the Technocrats seem to get along just fine without personified Avatars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T14:39:12-07:00","id":975239,"title":"","content":"Well, they have them, but they're either perceived differently or are simply not talked about because such things lead to reconditioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T15:15:26-07:00","id":975250,"title":"","content":"&quot;Technocrats do not have Avatars. Nobody claims to talk<br /> to dead gods or strange spirits before working on a scientific<br /> project. True Genius comes from within: The driving thoughts,<br /> the ideas that whisper tantalizingly, the dreams that form new<br /> directions. The benzene ring was realized in dreams; what\u2019s to say<br /> that the subconscious mind is without an understanding locked<br /> away from everyday thought? The idea of talking to a god or<br /> spirit for knowledge is an anachronism from shamanistic history.<br /> Modern scientists know that Genius comes from within&quot; ~ Guide to the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Genius is the Technocrat name for the Avatar Background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:45:31-07:00","id":975306,"title":"","content":"That's all Technocratic flavoring. You're effectively saying that enlightened Technocrats don't do magick, but enlightened science: it's the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T19:18:34-07:00","id":975333,"title":"","content":"Or is it? They're certainly mechanically similar. But it's also noted that Technocrats don't engage in seekings. Enlightenment simply HAPPENS at some point while they work on a problem.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the two things work the same for the sake of gameplay. But in game, are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T19:52:01-07:00","id":975342,"title":"","content":"Er... 'working on a very complicated and difficult problem and after working through it coming to an epiphany' is very likely to be... just the form that Technocratic Seekings take.<br /> <br /> Like, that's actually a valid description of what Traditionalist Seekings entail, even. A level of readiness is reached, the Mage undertakes trials mental or physical, and they finally gain understanding coupled with a heady feeling of accomplishment - or they fail, and instead have great disappointment.<br /> <br /> That doesn't sound <i>at all</i> like Technocrats not having Seekings.<br /> <br /> <br /> And for the purposes of setting, in truth, they're just <i>words</i> referring to seemingly common experiences for the gifted. Why do they happen? How do they happen? Is the &quot;Avatar&quot; for a Verbena even the same thing as the &quot;Avatar&quot; for an Akashic or a Dreamspeaker or a Technocrat or a Hermetic, or even that next Verbena down the street?<br /> <br /> And remember, the 'appearance' of the 'Avatar' and 'Seekings' varies from Mage to Mage, let alone from faction to faction. Some Mages don't seem to have a spiritual guide at all, and just end up doing things and reaching epiphanies on their own. That's not just Technocrats and not all Technocrats - Traditions Mages sometimes have Circumspect Avatars, and Demented Eidolon and Inner Knight are a Flaw and a Merit for a reason. Mage Storyteller's Handbook Revised gives example appearances for Avatars that are attached to Technocrats. Sometimes your muse is another person who just shows up from time to time, and sometimes it's your hat that you have to show off every time you cast a spell.<br /> <br /> Hell, it might just be that the only reason all these things are thought of as the same is because basically all of them agree there's <i>something</i> that lets them do all this crazy shit and decided to agree to the polite fiction that they have enough idea of what it is to stick a label on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-23-2016, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T19:58:07-07:00","id":975346,"title":"","content":"Yes! They do! They don't get to do things the easy way just by dint of being a Technocrat. They're still mages, no matter how they delude themselves. In fact, that's their whole schtick! Despite how the conduct this crusade against the magical elements of the world, they're actually a part of it.<br /> <br /> It's right there in the Guide to the Technocracy. While they may not go on mystical spirit journeys where they're tested by angels or whatever, they <i>do</i> undergo times of personal testing, where personal conundrums are contemplated or puzzles are solved in their dreams. Hell, they might even go on extra-dimensional style &quot;grail quests.&quot; So, Seekings. In fact, on page 137, under the header &quot;Seekings,&quot; the first line says &quot;Naturally, these visions appear in Technocratic Seekings as well.&quot; Go up one more header to the topic of Genius Eidolons, and it pretty much explicitly that they all have Avatars, which often manifest as guiding voices in their heads, and you shouldn't talk about it or else you get sent to Psych Ops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:56:52-07:00","id":975567,"title":"","content":"Quite Technocrats have Avatars - they are simply called Eidolons, and the Eidolon is simply usually associated with the voice of genius in a Technocrat's mind. As Frozenfishy said, while many Technocrats are unaware of even having an Avatar (Same goes in a way for Tradition Mages with weak avatars - they never really get to 'meet' them), some others know That Stranger telling them things, or see..strange things but decide not to report it - for their sake.<br /> <br /> Likewise, they have seekings. Sometimes by simply meditating on a problem and visualizing things in dreams, at other times by strokes of genius during work. It's the same for Mages, really, although I presume that Technocrats don't quite go on vision quests as much as the former.<br /> <br /> But the rules are the same, no matter what kind of Mage you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T12:25:35-07:00","id":975645,"title":"","content":"Sometimes the Avatar manifests as simple hunches, to the point where a Technocrat would never consciously know they were being directed. To them, it's all their own intuition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T15:55:31-07:00","id":975720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=975645#post975645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes the Avatar manifests as simple hunches, to the point where a Technocrat would never consciously know they were being directed. To them, it's all their own intuition.</div> </div> </div> </div>And sometimes it's this shadowed figure who pulls the Technocrat into an alley, gives him a fat envelope of essays, comments, odd jokes and questions, and says &quot;<i>I so wish we could spend some time with each other, but the damned Union would kill me and ruin you if they only knew I'm seeing you directly...be seeing you..someday.</i>&quot; before dissapearing.<br /> <br /> Technocrats can also get e-mails from their Avatars, perhaps of the &quot;This message will delete itself after you read it.&quot; kind. They can also get normal mail I suppose, but this doesn't seem techy enough :-P. Phone calls or SMSes would be cool.<br /> <br /> A Progenitor could meet his Avatar under the microscope (when he analyzes his own DNA), a Void Engineer in a star constellation that only he can find (but can show to others if they are patient and open-minded), and a Syndic in this one laconic, wise and understanding bar patron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-25-2016, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T17:03:53-07:00","id":975737,"title":"","content":"It's really really really easy to ditch Avatars altogether.<br /> <br /> You can even keep Seekings in the sense of epiphanies of the soul/Eureka! moments/shakabuku or just situations on which a mage's understanding of magic makes a quantum leap of degree. And do it as a part of the ongoing story instead of some weird off-camera dream-scaping exercise.<br /> <br /> They CAN be the heart and soul of the game, if that's specifically what you want and how the game is cast. Hells, the rules as is might not even go far enough. Instead of a rather crap Background where the crunch and fluff are out of whack and wildly disproportionate in how they affect the game, maybe Avatars could be as meaningful as, say, Geists are for Sin-Eaters.... Or maybe even as Shadows are to Wraiths. Why not create a system for &quot;Avatar-Guiding&quot; and let one of the other players take on the roll of your magical, occasionally asshole-ish, soul buddy?<br /> <br /> They can also get the way. A lot. There is a ton of stuff that can go on in Mage game and sometimes trying to insert having a bossy invisible friend/soul-stalker/weird cat from nowhere/vague feeling that &quot;that's not a moon&quot; just takes away from all the rest of the coolness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 09-25-2016, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T09:38:01-07:00","id":975973,"title":"","content":"That picture on the left side of the page when you post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:52:18-07:00","id":976467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=975973#post975973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That picture on the left side of the page when you post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing this for my next Virtual Adept NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:14:57-07:00","id":976558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=976467#post976467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm doing this for my next Virtual Adept NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your next VA NPC is going to have a quizzical or angry cube for a head?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:37:24-07:00","id":976606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=976558#post976558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"messag