Background where the crunch and fluff are out of whack and wildly disproportionate in how they affect the game, maybe Avatars could be as meaningful as, say, Geists are for Sin-Eaters.... Or maybe even as Shadows are to Wraiths. Why not create a system for &amp;quot;Avatar-Guiding&amp;quot; and let one of the other players take on the roll of your magical, occasionally asshole-ish, soul buddy?<br /> <br /> They can also get the way. A lot. There is a ton of stuff that can go on in Mage game and sometimes trying to insert having a bossy invisible friend/soul-stalker/weird cat from nowhere/vague feeling that &amp;quot;that's not a moon&amp;quot; just takes away from all the rest of the coolness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Avatar Guiding sounds really cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:20:45-07:00","id":977393,"title":"","content":"When I first came up with the idea, I blocked out a few notes on how to do it... Effectively how to &quot;build&quot; an Avatar somewhat like a Shadow. It ended up taking several Backgrounds out of play and made them a part of the Avatar, but looked like, as an idea, it could go somewhere. Then the group decided to go with a specific game where Avatars were ditched altogether. One character has a Totem that has made a couple of appearances and another character's mind is partitioning off, so he does talk to other aspects of himself which are very good at specific things, but they don't control his ability to warp reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T01:00:10-07:00","id":977654,"title":"","content":"I know according to both the Fallen from Demon and the Celestial Chorus, Avatars are pieces of &quot;the One&quot; as in when God/Whatever &quot;smote the cosmos&quot; it was broken into pieces itself, many of which fused with human souls to make mages, and others later causing the torrent of Avatars in the Avatar Storms in the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:13:54-07:00","id":977773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=977654#post977654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know according to both the Fallen from Demon and the Celestial Chorus, Avatars are pieces of &quot;the One&quot; as in when God/Whatever &quot;smote the cosmos&quot; it was broken into pieces itself, many of which fused with human souls to make mages, and others later causing the torrent of Avatars in the Avatar Storms in the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Demon is... problematic to take as canon. While I do like it as possibly the <i>only</i> splat that can provide some kind of cohesive World of Darkness that ties all splats together, taking what Demon (which is a game that explicitly says that prehistory existed as multiple things all at once so it's up to interpretations) says about Mage (a game that is quite literally about things being dependent on interpretation) hardly gives concrete answers.<br /> <br /> For example, Demon states that God created Man to be &quot;as God,&quot; but the angels didn't know what exactly that meant. They only knew that early man was effectively &quot;asleep,&quot; hardly more sentient than animals. In an attempt to save them from themselves, early angels force &quot;woke up&quot; early humans so as to give them agency and a way to save themselves from an impending mysterious doom.<br /> <br /> Now, this can be interpreted biblically as the the serpent tempting Adam and Eve into eating of the Tree of Knowledge, or concerned angels giving the early tribes of barely evolved mankind actual sentience. As far as Demon is concerned, they're both the same things, and myriad others. However, it can also be interpreted that these angels Awakened, in the Mage sense, mankind to its inherent power that it always had. This was also <b>before</b> any of the cosmic calamities that sent the World of Darkness careening to the dark place that it is, but it could have been the start of it. &quot;God,&quot; whatever it really was or could be interpreted as, was still around and kicking in this time.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that maybe Demons (formerly the angels) think that Avatars <i>are</i> some kind of shard of The One, and this is what gives mages their power. I don't specifically recall reading that, but I'm also not the most well read when it comes to the Demon books after the part where their history component ends. However, Demon also implies that humans were created to have reality altering power in the first place. Of course, they could also <i>not</i> have been created deliberately at all, depending on how liberally you interpret Demon prehistory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:33:47-07:00","id":977806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=977773#post977773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Demon is... problematic to take as canon. While I do like it as possibly the <i>only</i> splat that can provide some kind of cohesive World of Darkness that ties all splats together, taking what Demon (which is a game that explicitly says that prehistory existed as multiple things all at once so it's up to interpretations) says about Mage (a game that is quite literally about things being dependent on interpretation) hardly gives concrete answers.<br /> <br /> For example, Demon states that God created Man to be &quot;as God,&quot; but the angels didn't know what exactly that meant. They only knew that early man was effectively &quot;asleep,&quot; hardly more sentient than animals. In an attempt to save them from themselves, early angels force &quot;woke up&quot; early humans so as to give them agency and a way to save themselves from an impending mysterious doom.<br /> <br /> Now, this can be interpreted biblically as the the serpent tempting Adam and Eve into eating of the Tree of Knowledge, or concerned angels giving the early tribes of barely evolved mankind actual sentience. As far as Demon is concerned, they're both the same things, and myriad others. However, it can also be interpreted that these angels Awakened, in the Mage sense, mankind to its inherent power that it always had. This was also <b>before</b> any of the cosmic calamities that sent the World of Darkness careening to the dark place that it is, but it could have been the start of it. &quot;God,&quot; whatever it really was or could be interpreted as, was still around and kicking in this time.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that maybe Demons (formerly the angels) think that Avatars <i>are</i> some kind of shard of The One, and this is what gives mages their power. I don't specifically recall reading that, but I'm also not the most well read when it comes to the Demon books after the part where their history component ends. However, Demon also implies that humans were created to have reality altering power in the first place. Of course, they could also <i>not</i> have been created deliberately at all, depending on how liberally you interpret Demon prehistory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah valid points to be sure, and yes, taking it as the gospel of canon is also iffy. It's still just one of many takes on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:15:59-07:00","id":977853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=977806#post977806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah valid points to be sure, and yes, taking it as the gospel of canon is also iffy. It's still just one of many takes on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does tackle the question in the related fiction in at least a way. A Halaku finds his scythe in the hands of a Euthanatos that is part of a cabal and he DEFINITELY sees the Avatars of the mages as being what's left of the &quot;souls&quot; of the Angels that died in the wars up to the Fall. And the &quot;angel bits&quot; are spliced on to the human souls. And he uses his scythe to cut the angel-y bits free, much to the unhappiness of the mages involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:57:57-07:00","id":977916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=977853#post977853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does tackle the question in the related fiction in at least a way. A Halaku finds his scythe in the hands of a Euthanatos that is part of a cabal and he DEFINITELY sees the Avatars of the mages as being what's left of the &quot;souls&quot; of the Angels that died in the wars up to the Fall. And the &quot;angel bits&quot; are spliced on to the human souls. And he uses his scythe to cut the angel-y bits free, much to the unhappiness of the mages involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that is part of what I was referring to in my first post. He is outraged that humans have stolen angelic souls to gain forbidden knowledge and power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:12:36-07:00","id":977928,"title":"","content":"My main problem with Demon is how irritatingly hard it is to permakill demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:58:07-07:00","id":977984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974131-what-is-an-avatar?p=977806#post977806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah valid points to be sure, and yes, taking it as the gospel of canon is also iffy. It's still just one of many takes on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can't really take Anything as gospel of canon in WOD, even within the same game-line. If you were to ask 11 denizens of WOD the same question, you'd get 37 different answers and a migraine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:23:48-07:00","id":978000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m